{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSup9ZW9cNdqRVwWRetf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Linking creates symlinks in `00_data/rnaseq_bulk/raw/` that point at your source files. Your FASTQs are never copied, moved or modified. Once linking is done, the finalize step:\n\n- **Checks integrity.** By default (`quick`) it confirms each link resolves, each file is non-empty and each file starts with valid gzip data. `full` mode also decompresses every file, but only if you ask for it.\n- **Writes `files.csv`.** This has one row per sample and lane, with paths to the linked R1/R2 files. The script owns it and it is read-only on disk.\n- **Writes `samples.csv`.** This has one row per sample, with `sample_id` filled in and the design columns (`condition`, `group`, `replicate`) left blank for you to complete.\n- **Fills in the project's `CONTEXT.md` and `HISTORY.md`.** It also records which integrity mode was used.\n\nThe stage does no QC, analysis or interpretation of the data. To analyse only some samples later, delete their rows from `samples.csv`. The links stay in place, so you can undo that choice.\n\nConfirm to create symlinks under 00_data/rnaseq_bulk/raw/, or provide a different path."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":438,"cache_read_input_tokens":36301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":438},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68f70388-5480-59f1-82ab-dece295adbdd","uuid":"94db65cf-024a-48f2-bd41-2e29b41a8289","timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:37:22.782Z","request_id":"req_011CgSup9GeL1miokMjT9eA6"}
